## The start of my coding experience (cca 2025) - Commit system
In Slovakia, for the Astronomical Observatory in Kolonica, I made a simple Tkinter Python program for controlling a USB surge protector using AI. It worked; I added more features to it.
But everything was copy-pasted from an AI chat, and that AI was often "stupid", it was simply hard to do.


## Discovery of PRs and Claude Code (2026)
I wanted to add support for some Waste Collector to mampfes/hacs-waste-collection-schedule, and that is the first time I used Google Antigravity; I was amazed, but then I reached my limit.
That is approximately when i discovered PRs.
Then i continued contributing to mampfes/hacs-waste-collection-schedule with Google Gemini and thanks to amazing maintainers of mampfes/hacs-waste-collection-schedule i discovered Claude Code, that chenged everything!
Thank you very much **credits here**!
So that is when everything changed.
- I no longer used commits but PRs
- I made more and more programs with that amazing agentic AI including visual-astro (worth menitiong i discovered Lovable few months before Claude Code)
- The AI (Claude Code) was smarter, workid with GitHub directly and even more

## Discovery of CodeRabbit (few days ago)
And now, few days ago, i discovered CodeRabbit (yeah, AI started talking with AI under my eyes)
It was free and found bugs in Claude Code code that was good but now is EVEN better.
Also worth mentioning that few weeks ago i discovered Vercel previews wich helped with my web apps like visual-astro - i no longer needed to merge in order to see if it looks like it hsould.


